          A 70 pint dehumidifier is two different things depending on who is selling it. On a portable, it is the old rating for what the 2019 DOE test now calls a 50 pint machine. On a crawl space unit from AprilAire or Santa Fe, it is a genuine 70 pints at AHAM conditions, from a contractor-grade box that costs several times as much. This guide sorts the two, shows the cooler-air figures each maker publishes, and picks seven units worth buying.
