          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If you wanted the classic 70 pint portable, buy the Frigidaire FHDD5034Y1, or the Honeywell TPFIT50PWK with its pump, knowing a 50 pint machine by today's test is the same class and as large as a portable gets. If you need a genuinely bigger dehumidifier for a crawl space or a large, cool basement, the AprilAire E070 and Santa Fe Compact70 are the true 70 pint units to buy, and the AlorAir Sentinels are the better choice where temperatures fall into the 40s.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whichever way you go, check which test the pints come from, ignore saturation figures, plan the drainage before you order and set the humidistat to about 50%. Fix any liquid water first, and the right size of dehumidifier will do the rest.
